   "hypothesis_id": "hyp2",
   "mechanism": "EIF2AK4 (GCN2) functions as an amino acid sensor that drives metabolic rewiring in immune cells. In the epidermis, the activity of this pathway influences IL-17A production by resident γδ T cells. Specific genetic variants, such as rs182525087, are significantly associated with a decreased risk of psoriasis, likely by modulating this inflammatory signaling axis.",
